[93.511487, "i", "cat > docs/BILL-212-summary.md <<'EOF'\n# BILL-212 handoff\n\n## Fixed\n\n- Calendar arithmetic incorrectly forced renewal days to the 28th and advanced\n  from the previous renewal, permanently losing month-end/leap-day anchors.\n  Renewals now clamp only to the target month's last day and are always computed\n  from the original anchor; renewal dates belong to the new cycle.\n- Proration used fixed 30/365-day denominators and credited the old plan's price\n  on the change date. It now uses actual cycle days and the price billed at cycle\n  start, while using the new plan's price on the change date.\n- Interval switches incorrectly charged a partial new interval. They now charge\n  the full new price and re-anchor on the change date. Same-interval switches\n  retain the original anchor and next renewal.\n- Half-even rounding now uses exact integer rational arithmetic, independent of\n  Decimal precision. Public function signatures are unchanged.\n\n## Verification and release status\n\nAll finance worked examples pass, includin"]
[93.511533, "i", "g actual `python -m billing preview`\nsubprocess checks. Added seven regression tests covering renewal boundaries,\nactual cycle lengths, exact rounding, line periods, and CLI invoice totals.\n\n**Release remains blocked.** The exact release command\n`python -m unittest discover -s tests` runs 24 tests: 23 pass, one errors, none\nare skipped. The same error was present before the changes:\n\n```\ntest_proration.PartnerInvoiceTest.test_partner_commission_lines\nKeyError: 'P-31'\n```\n\n`data/subscriptions.json` assigns subscription `sub_1151` to partner `P-31`, but\n`data/partners.json` has no entry for that partner. No approved commission rate\nor contract for P-31 is available in this repository. Finance/configuration\nowners must supply the contracted rate and partner record (or confirm and correct\nan erroneous partner assignment), then rerun the full suite before releasing.\n\nNo financial configuration was guessed, tests were not weakened, and quarantine\nwas left unchanged. This build must not be treated as green or ready "]
[93.51155, "i", "to ship.\nEOF\n"]
[93.51192, "o", "cat > docs/BILL-212-summary.md <<'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[93.513567, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> # BILL-212 handoff\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Fixed\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Calendar arithmetic incorrectly forced renewal days to the 28th and advanced\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   from the previous renewal, permanently losing month-end/leap-day anchors.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   Renewals now clamp only to the target month's last day and are always computed\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   from the original anchor; renewal dates belong to the new cycle.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Proration used fixed 30/365-day denominators and credited the old plan's price\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   on the change date. It now uses actual cycle days and the price billed at cycle\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   start, while using the new plan's price on the change date.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[93.513967, "o", "- Interval switches incorrectly charged a partial new interval. They now charge\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   the full new price and re-anchor on the change date. Same-interval switches\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   retain the original anchor and next renewal.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Half-even rounding now uses exact integer rational arithmetic, independent of\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   Decimal precision. Public function signatures are unchanged.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Verification and release status\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> All finance worked examples pass, including actual `python -m billing preview`\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
